/target/
*.compiled.json.tmp
# Review artifacts a run writes under the invocation directory: the last-green
# baseline drift is measured against, and the candidate rows a human reviews.
# Ignored here because the only runs invoked from runner/ are the fixture and
# mega-sample suites, whose baselines are scratch. A consumer repo that wants
# cross-run drift detection commits its own .harness/ — see
# docs/drift-and-accept.md.
/.harness/
# The web half of the cross-surface parity gate: `scenarios/parity.yaml` writes
# it from the live page on every run, so it is an output, not a fixture. Its
# counterpart `baselines/parity.ios.txt` IS committed — that surface has no
# producer here.
/samples/web-fixture/baselines/parity.web.txt
# The live iOS capture `samples/ios-fixture/scenarios/settings-list.yaml`
# writes on every run; `expected/settings-list.txt` is the committed half.
/samples/ios-fixture/baselines/
# The screen baselines the game samples' first run records next to each
# scenario. They belong to the host that recorded them: a device run and a
# FakeMirroring run see different screens, so one host's baseline is the
# other's drift. Each run starts from none and records its own.
/samples/game-shell/scenarios/*.ios.compiled.json
/samples/game-result/scenarios/*.ios.compiled.json
